1
00:01:27,355 --> 00:01:38,688
<v WOMAN> Jack, I'm thinking of taking the kids to the seaside on a surfing holiday this summer and I wanted to ask your advice - as I know you're such an expert.

2
00:01:38,698 --> 00:01:43,862
<v JACK> Well, I don't know about that, but yes, I've done a bit of surfing over the years.

3
00:01:43,872 --> 00:01:45,969
<v JACK> I'd thoroughly recommend it.

4
00:01:45,979 --> 00:01:50,309
<v JACK> I think it's the kind of holiday all the family can enjoy together.

5
00:01:50,319 --> 00:01:55,828
<v JACK> The thing about surfing is that it's great for all ages and all abilities.

6
00:01:55,838 --> 00:01:58,856
<v JACK> My youngest started when he was only three!

7
00:01:58,866 --> 00:02:03,917
<v WOMAN> Wow! But it's quite physically demanding, isn't it?

8
00:02:03,927 --> 00:02:06,566
<v WOMAN> I've heard you need to be pretty fit.

9
00:02:06,576 --> 00:02:11,176
<v JACK> Yes. You'll certainly learn more quickly and won't tire as easily.

10
00:02:11,186 --> 00:02:13,697
<v WOMAN> Well - that should be OK for us.

11
00:02:13,707 --> 00:02:17,620
<v WOMAN> You've been surfing a few times in Ireland, haven't you?

12
00:02:17,630 --> 00:02:22,989
<v JACK> Yes. There's some great surfing there, which people don't always realise.

13
00:02:22,999 --> 00:02:28,459
<v WOMAN> And which locations would you recommend? - there seem to be quite a few.

14
00:02:28,469 --> 00:02:29,778
<v JACK> Yes, there are loads.

15
00:02:29,788 --> 00:02:32,484
<v JACK> Last year we went to County Donegal.

16
00:02:32,494 --> 00:02:35,420
<v JACK> There are several great places to surf there.

17
00:02:35,430 --> 00:02:38,309
<v WOMAN> What about in County Clare?

18
00:02:38,319 --> 00:02:41,767
<v WOMAN> I read that's also really good for surfing.

19
00:02:41,777 --> 00:02:43,225
<v JACK> Yes, it is.

20
00:02:43,235 --> 00:02:45,052
<v JACK> I've been there a few times.

21
00:02:45,062 --> 00:02:46,943
<v JACK> Most people go to Lahinch.

22
00:02:46,953 --> 00:02:48,732
<v JACK> My kids love it there.

23
00:02:48,742 --> 00:02:52,463
<v JACK> The waves aren't too challenging and the town is very lively.

24
00:02:52,473 --> 00:02:54,871
<v WOMAN> Are there good hotels there?

25
00:02:54,881 --> 00:03:01,304
<v JACK> Yes - some very nice ones and there are also a few basic hostels and campsites.

26
00:03:01,304 --> 00:03:05,675
<v JACK> It's great if you need lessons as the surf schools are excellent.

27
00:03:05,685 --> 00:03:06,922
<v WOMAN> Sounds good.

28
00:03:06,932 --> 00:03:13,773
<v JACK> Yes and there's lots to see in the area - like those well-known cliffs - ... I've forgotten the name of them ...

29
00:03:13,783 --> 00:03:16,543
<v WOMAN> Oh don't worry - I can look them up.

30
00:03:16,553 --> 00:03:23,850
<v JACK> I've also been surfing in County Mayo, which is less well-known for surfing, but we had a really good time.

31
00:03:23,860 --> 00:03:27,236
<v JACK> That was a few years ago when the kids were younger.

32
00:03:27,246 --> 00:03:30,926
<v JACK> There's a good surf school at Carrowniskey beach.

33
00:03:30,936 --> 00:03:32,507
<v WOMAN> How do you spell that?

34
00:03:32,517 --> 00:03:43,024
<v JACK> C-A-double R-O-W-N-I-S-K-E-Y.

35
00:03:43,034 --> 00:03:44,302
<v WOMAN> ОK.

36
00:03:44,312 --> 00:03:49,819
<v JACK> I put the kids into the surf camp they run during the summer for 10-16 year olds.

37
00:03:49,829 --> 00:03:53,088
<v WOMAN> Oh right. How long was that for?

38
00:03:53,098 --> 00:03:55,690
<v JACK> Three hours every day for a week.

39
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:59,453
<v JACK> It was perfect - they were so tired out after that.

40
00:03:59,463 --> 00:04:00,893
<v WOMAN> I can imagine.

41
00:04:00,903 --> 00:04:08,641
<v JACK> One thing we did while the kids were surfing was to rent some kayaks to have a look around the bay which is nearby.

42
00:04:08,651 --> 00:04:10,253
<v JACK> It's really beautiful.

43
00:04:10,263 --> 00:04:12,303
<v WOMAN> Oh, I'd love to do that.

44
00:04:48,123 --> 00:04:53,549
<v WOMAN> Now the only time I went to Ireland it rained practically every day.

45
00:04:53,559 --> 00:04:58,465
<v JACK> Mmm yes - that can be a problem - but you can surf in the rain, you know.

46
00:04:58,475 --> 00:05:01,636
<v WOMAN> It doesn't have the same appeal, somehow.

47
00:05:01,646 --> 00:05:11,037
<v JACK> Well, the weather's been fine the last couple of years when I've been there, but actually, it tends to rain more in August than in the spring or autumn.

48
00:05:11,047 --> 00:05:15,388
<v JACK> September's my favourite month because the water is warmer then.

49
00:05:15,398 --> 00:05:19,377
<v WOMAN> The only problem is that the kids are back to school then.

50
00:05:19,387 --> 00:05:25,169
<v JACK> I know. But one good thing about Irish summers is that it doesn't get too hot.

51
00:05:25,179 --> 00:05:32,906
<v JACK> The average temperature is about 19 degrees and it usually doesn't go above 25 degrees.

52
00:05:32,916 --> 00:05:34,556
<v WOMAN> That sounds alright.

53
00:05:34,566 --> 00:05:36,644
<v WOMAN> Now what about costs?

54
00:05:36,654 --> 00:05:42,535
<v JACK> Surfing is a pretty cheap holiday really - the only cost is the hire of equipment.

55
00:05:42,545 --> 00:05:54,247
<v JACK> You can expect to pay a daily rate of about 30 euros for the hire of a wetsuit and board - but you can save about 40 euros if you hire by the week.

56
00:05:54,257 --> 00:05:55,438
<v WOMAN> That's not too bad.

57
00:05:55,448 --> 00:06:02,609
<v JACK> No. It's important to make sure you get good quality wetsuits - you'll all get too cold if you don't.

58
00:06:02,619 --> 00:06:05,869
<v JACK> And make sure you also get boots.

59
00:06:05,879 --> 00:06:10,599
<v JACK> They keep your feet warm and it's easier to surf with them on too.

60
00:06:10,609 --> 00:06:13,569
<v WOMAN> OK. Well, thanks very much …